Ukraine is not a NATO member and though  the West is supporting Ukrainian forces  we're not engaged in direct combat with  Russia if there has been a deliberate  attack on NATO soil though that could  change and Canada a NATO member would be  part of it our Ottawa bureau chief  Mercedes Stevenson is with me Mercedes  it is a tense time what are the next  steps in terms of NATO's response  it is Donna and what's expected next  from all of the sources I've spoken to  is that there may be Article 4 invoked  that's basically a meeting and it's a  meeting that happens whenever member  states feel that their territorial  Integrity or security might be  threatened it's very different than  article 5. Article 5 is an attack on one  is an attack on all and that's only been  invoked once in NATO history and that  was by the United States after 9 11. but  even Article 5 is not an automatic Call  to Arms for those who are feeling  anxious about what's happening tonight  there's a lot of discussion that would  have to happen and a lot of belief that  this would have to have been deliberate  and worth a military response before  that would happen one of the senior  folks in the military who I was spoken  speaking to earlier tonight said to me  look if we put this into Russia's hands  and allowed them to decide what the  trigger was was something as simple as a  single strike we would be out of control  the reality is at the end of the day  this will largely be decided by the  United States of America and of course  it will depend on whether or not this  was a deliberate or an accidental strike  and that's something that really is  still being determined at this point so  likely at this point Donna that it would  be article four not Article 5 which is  basically a meeting that's been invoked  seven times before in fact it was also  invoked when Russia initially invaded  Ukraine by seven NATO members who were  concerned about their territorial  Integrity including Poland this would  not be the first time that Russia has  potentially accidentally struck a  country that is not Ukraine they hit  Moldova back in October but there was  less discussion on that because Moldova  is not a NATO country the military  sources I spoke to also told me the  Russians have largely run out of  precision Munitions they are using  dumber and dumber bombs and they don't  have great discipline or leadership  which could account for a strike so of  course we're waiting to find out what  happened but all those things come into  consideration what is Canada's response  at this stage  well Donna at this point it's pretty  muted we heard from Melanie Jolie who is  the Minister of Foreign Affairs she's at  the G20 uh very recently take a listen  to what she had to say  so obviously we're following up this  situation very closely uh we're in  contact with Poland as well as with our  partners  um my heart is with the family and loved  ones of the victims and also with the  people of Poland just kind of believe  this triggers article 5.  we're following up this situation very  closely and of course we'll be having  important meetings today with allies  so as you can see there Donna very very  careful there's a lot of phone calls I'm  told by senior officials going on behind  the scenes to the United States Poland  NATO and even they're trying to find out  from Russia what may have happened here  but right now everyone is being very  careful with their words a reminder  there are 40 Canadian combat engineers  currently in Poland but there's of  course no suggestion that they were  involved anywhere near the strike but  for those wondering about Canadian  Forces there that's who's in the region  all right Mercedes Stevenson in Ottawa  thanks
 

